{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-16T17:21:57Z","content":"I noticed why the files and the README were not showing up on your GitHub repository. \n\nBecause `canteen-app` was initialized with its own `.git` folder inside it, the parent Git repository treated it as a **git submodule (nested repository)**. Consequently, Git registered a link to the folder but did not track or upload any of the actual files inside it (leaving it empty on GitHub, and preventing the README from rendering).\n\nI have run the necessary commands to fix this:\n1. **Removed the nested `.git` folder** from inside `canteen-app/` so Git stops treating it as a submodule.\n2. **Untracked the submodule placeholder** in the parent repository.\n3. **Staged and committed all project files** (your code, styles, configuration) as normal files.\n4. **Copied the `README.md` to the root directory** so GitHub can find it and render it on your main repository home page!\n\nI am now running the `git push origin main` command in the background to upload these changes. I will update you as soon as the push finishes!"}
