{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-16T17:45:04Z","content":"I have copied all the project files, including the **`README.md`** and the mockup image, directly into your root **`canteen-app`** folder! \n\nThe reason you didn't see the README before was because it was only in the `scratch/canteen-app` folder. Now, both folders are fully synced.\n\n---\n\n### 💻 Run these commands in your MINGW64 Terminal:\n\nCopy and paste these commands step-by-step to clean up Git from your AppData folder and push the clean project:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Ensure you are in the AppData directory\ncd ~/.gemini/antigravity\n\n# Step 2: Delete Git tracking from the AppData directory (critical for privacy!)\nrm -rf .git\n\n# Step 3: Enter the actual project directory\ncd canteen-app\n\n# Step 4: Verify the README.md and files are visible\nls -la\n```\n*(You will now see `README.md` listed right there in your console!)*\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Step 5: Push the project to GitHub\n\nOnce you see the files, run these commands inside the `canteen-app` folder to push it:\n\n```bash\n# Initialize clean Git tracking inside the project folder\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: initial commit for GlassCanteen\"\n\n# Link to GitHub and push\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/techmarshal03/glass-canteen.git\ngit push -u origin main -f\n```\n\nOnce this push completes, open `https://github.com/techmarshal03/glass-canteen` and you will see all your project files and the gorgeous markdown README displayed right on the home page!"}
